<title>HUNGARY: Hungary cenbank to quote c.Euro currencies.</title>
<headline>Hungary cenbank to quote c.Euro currencies.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) will add three central European currencies to those for which it quotes exchange rates but will stop quoting the Kuwaiti dinar and the Irish pound, the NBH said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bank will quote the Czech crown, the Slovak crown and the Polish zloty.</p>
<p>The move will go into effect on April 1, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The move results from the developments of economic relations and commitments that Hungary undertook with its OECD membership,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Hungary became an OECD member in March 1996.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
